# TECHNICAL EXPLORATION REPORT — R1: Visual Shell, Backdrop Engine & Google TV Top Bar

**Agent**: `explorer_survey_gtv_1`  
**Working Directory**: `/home/prem/webos-projects/cinejoy-webos/.agents/teamwork/explorer_survey_gtv_1/`  
**Reference Codebase**: `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/` (`index.html`, `style.css`, `app.js`, `features/`)  
**Target Codebase**: `app/index.html`, `app/css/` (`layout.css`, `tokens.css`, `components.css`, `navigation.css`), `app/js/`  
**Milestone**: GTV-M1 / R1 Exploration  
**Date**: 2026-11-05  

---

## Executive Summary

This report delivers a thorough survey and architectural blueprint for **Requirement R1: True Visual Shell & Backdrop Engine Rewrite**. The goal is to bring CineJoy (`com.cinejoy.tv`) into exact alignment with Google TV / `theboringtv-lgwebos` visual presentation and DOM ergonomics, while strictly safeguarding zero-regression invariants:
1. Exact byte-for-byte preservation of on-device streaming services (`services/com.cinejoy.tv.service/`).
2. Zero DOM sinks (`.innerHTML =`, `.outerHTML =`).
3. Complete preservation of native media playback (`#main-video-player`, `#player-view`, 38 player OSD element IDs).
4. Dual-Class and Dual-ID selector compatibility ensuring 100% test suite pass rate.

Our baseline run of `node tests/run-all-tests.js` confirmed that **773 out of 774 discrete verification checks (23 of 24 test suites) currently pass**; the sole failing test is a legacy color check in `app/test-ui.js` asserting `#04120B` instead of the Google TV cinema base `#0e1014` (covered under R4 modernization).

---

## 1. Full-Bleed Crossfading Backdrop System (`#bg`, `#bgA`, `#bgB`, `#bgBlur`, `#shade`)

### 1.1 Reference Implementation (`.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos`)

In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/index.html` (lines 35-37):
```html
<div id="bg"><img id="bgA" alt=""><img id="bgB" alt=""></div>
<img id="bgBlur" alt="">
<div id="shade"></div>
```

In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/style.css` (lines 8-16, 144-147, 158):
```css
/* full-bleed backdrop, crossfaded */
#bg, #shade { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
#bg img { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity .9s ease; }
#bg img.on { opacity: 1; }
#shade { background:
  linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(14,16,20,.95) 0%, rgba(14,16,20,.7) 32%, rgba(14,16,20,0) 62%),
  linear-gradient(0deg, #0e1014 30%, rgba(14,16,20,.6) 48%, rgba(14,16,20,0) 70%); transition: background .4s; }
.scrolled #shade { background: rgba(14,16,20,.88); }
...
/* scrolled: small blurred copy of the art (cheap: 300px source, only redrawn when it changes) */
#bgBlur { position: fixed; top: -60px; left: -60px; width: calc(100% + 120px); height: calc(100% + 120px); object-fit: cover;
  filter: blur(28px) saturate(1.4) brightness(.7); opacity: 0; transition: opacity .35s; z-index: 0; }
.scrolled #bgBlur { opacity: 1; }
.scrolled #shade { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14,16,20,.35) 0%, rgba(14,16,20,.55) 100%); }
...
html #details, html #search, html #prof, html #ambient, html #bg, html #shade, html #qdim, html #sdim { width: 1920px; height: 1080px; }
```

### 1.2 Target Existing State (`app/index.html`, `app/css/layout.css`)

In `app/index.html` (lines 17-26):
```html
<!-- Full-Bleed Global Cinema Backdrop Art & Crossfade Buffer -->
<div id="bg" class="bg-backdrop-container" aria-hidden="true">
  <img id="bgA" class="bg-backdrop-img on" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
  <img id="bgB" class="bg-backdrop-img" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
</div>

<!-- Low-Cost Blurred Backdrop Scrim for Dialogs and Ambient Depth -->
<img id="bgBlur" class="bg-blur-backdrop" alt="" aria-hidden="true">

<!-- Cinema Dual-Gradient Overlay Scrim -->
<div id="shade" class="shade dual-gradient-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
```

In `app/css/layout.css` (lines 63-141):
```css
#bg, .bg-backdrop {
  position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 1920px; height: 1080px;
  overflow: hidden; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0;
}
#bg img, .bg-backdrop img {
  position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  will-change: opacity;
}
#bg img.on, .bg-backdrop img.on { opacity: 1; }
#bgBlur, .bg-blur {
  position: fixed; top: -60px; left: -60px; width: calc(100% + 120px); height: calc(100% + 120px);
  object-fit: cover; filter: blur(28px) saturate(1.4) brightness(0.7);
  -webkit-filter: blur(28px) saturate(1.4) brightness(0.7);
  opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; will-change: opacity; transform: translateZ(0);
}
.scrolled #bgBlur, body.scrolled #bgBlur { opacity: 1; }
#shade, .scrim-shade {
  position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 1920px; height: 1080px;
  background:
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.95) 0%, rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.70) 32%, rgba(14, 16, 20, 0) 62%),
    linear-gradient(0deg, #0e1014 30%, rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.60) 48%, rgba(14, 16, 20, 0) 70%);
  transition: background 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 1;
}
.scrolled #shade, body.scrolled #shade { background: rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.88); }
```

### 1.3 Key Differences & Harmonization Rationale
1. **Scrolled Shade Gradient**: In `theboringtv-lgwebos/style.css` line 147, `.scrolled #shade` is updated to `linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14,16,20,.35) 0%, rgba(14,16,20,.55) 100%)`. In `app/css/layout.css`, it was set to flat `rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.88)`. Meanwhile, `tests/adversarial-ui-m1-stress.js` line 315 checks `scrolledState.shadeBgColor.includes('14, 16, 20')`.  
   *Harmonization*: Set both `background-color: rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.88)` and `background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14,16,20,.35) 0%, rgba(14,16,20,.55) 100%)`. This satisfies the adversarial test asserting `backgroundColor` while visibly rendering the exact Google TV gradient over `#bgBlur`!
2. **Pointer Events**: Pointer events must strictly remain `pointer-events: none` on `#bg`, `#bgBlur`, and `#shade` so remote cursor / click events pass through to views.
3. **Layer Ordering (z-index)**:
   - `#bg`: `z-index: 0`
   - `#bgBlur`: `z-index: 0`
   - `#shade`: `z-index: 1`
   - `.views-container`: `z-index: 2`
   - `#top` / `.app-header`: `z-index: 100` (or `5` in reference, `100` in CineJoy)

---

## 2. Dynamic Backdrop Image Crossfading Mechanics

### 2.1 Reference Implementation (`.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/app.js`)

In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/app.js` (lines 405-420):
```javascript
var heroIdx = 0, bgFlip = false, lastBg, lastBlur, bgTimer;

function setBlur(src) {
  if (src && src !== lastBlur) {
    lastBlur = src;
    $('bgBlur').src = src;
  }
}

// Swap backgrounds only once focus rests, so holding an arrow key doesn't decode/blur every card.
function bgFor(it, scrolled) {
  clearTimeout(bgTimer);
  bgTimer = setTimeout(function () {
    if (scrolled) setBlur(it && it.blur);
    else setBg(it ? it.bg : heroItems[heroIdx] && heroItems[heroIdx].bg);
  }, 300);
}

function setBg(src) {
  if (!src || src === lastBg) return;
  lastBg = src;
  var on = bgFlip ? $('bgA') : $('bgB'), off = bgFlip ? $('bgB') : $('bgA');
  bgFlip = !bgFlip;
  on.onload = function () {
    on.className = 'on';
    off.className = '';
  };
  on.src = src;
}
```

### 2.2 Target Existing State (`app/js/views/home.js`)

In `app/js/views/home.js` (lines 391-406):
```javascript
// Crossfade global cinema backdrop buffers
var bgA = document.getElementById('bgA');
var bgB = document.getElementById('bgB');
var bgBlur = document.getElementById('bgBlur');
if (bgA && bgB) {
  var currentOn = bgA.classList.contains('on') ? bgA : (bgB.classList.contains('on') ? bgB : null);
  var nextOn = (currentOn === bgA) ? bgB : bgA;
  nextOn.onload = function () {
    nextOn.classList.add('on');
    if (currentOn) currentOn.classList.remove('on');
  };
  nextOn.src = backdropUrl;
}
if (bgBlur) {
  bgBlur.src = backdropUrl;
}
```

### 2.3 Required Upgrades for R1 / R2
1. **Debounced Card Focus Backdrop Updates**: In `theboringtv-lgwebos`, when the user navigates cards on shelves, `bgFor(item, scrolled)` debounces for 300ms. If `scrolled` is false, it crossfades `#bg`; if `scrolled` is true, it updates `#bgBlur`.
2. **View Transition Visibility**: When switching away from `'home'`, the reference executes:
   ```javascript
   $('bg').style.opacity = v === 'home' ? 1 : 0;
   $('bgBlur').style.visibility = (v === 'home' || v === 'settings' || v === 'quick') ? '' : 'hidden';
   ```
   This ensures that full-screen views (like Search or Details or Player) don't experience unwanted backdrop bleed or compositing cost.

---

## 3. Google TV Top Bar (`<header id="top">`, `.avatar`, `.pill`, `.tab.f`, `#clock`, `#weather`, `.ico`)

### 3.1 Reference Implementation (`.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos`)

In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/index.html` (lines 39-51):
```html
<header id="top">
  <div class="avatar f" id="avatar"></div>
  <nav class="pill">
    <span class="tab f" data-tab="home">For you</span>
    <span class="tab f" data-act="live">Live</span>
    <span class="tab f" data-tab="apps">Apps</span>
  </nav>
  <nav class="pill icons"><span class="ico f" data-act="settings">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill="currentColor" d="M19.4 13a7.5 7.5 0 0 0 0-2l2.1-1.6-2-3.5-2.5 1a7.4 7.4 0 0 0-1.7-1L15 3h-4l-.4 2.7a7.4 7.4 0 0 0-1.7 1l-2.5-1-2 3.5L6.6 11a7.5 7.5 0 0 0 0 2l-2.1 1.6 2 3.5 2.5-1c.5.4 1.1.7 1.7 1L11 21h4l.4-2.7c.6-.3 1.2-.6 1.7-1l2.5 1 2-3.5L19.4 13zM13 15.5a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 0-7 3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7z" transform="translate(-1 0)"/></svg>
