### 3.2 Target Existing Header (`app/index.html` lines 29-62)
Currently in CineJoy:
- `<header id="app-header" class="app-header" role="banner">`
- Left brand container `#header-brand` with SVG icon and text "CINEJOY"
- `<nav id="header-nav" class="nav-glass-pill pill">` with 4 links:
  - `#header-nav-home` (Home)
  - `#header-nav-movies` (Movies)
  - `#header-nav-series` (Series)
  - `#header-nav-search` (Search)
- No `.avatar` profile indicator.
- No `.pill.icons` with `.ico`.
- No `#weather` element.
- No `#clock` live time element.
- Auto-hide `.scrolled` styling exists in `layout.css`, but the `.scrolled` class is never toggled at runtime in `app/js/`.

### 3.3 Recommended Google TV Top Bar Structure for CineJoy
To fulfill Requirement R1 while preserving all test assertions:
```html
<header id="top" class="app-header" role="banner">
  <!-- Profile Avatar Indicator -->
  <div class="avatar f" id="avatar" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" tabindex="-1">C</div>

  <!-- Google TV Glass Navigation Pill -->
  <nav id="header-nav" class="pill" role="navigation">
    <a id="header-nav-home" href="#home" class="tab f nav-pill-item active" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" data-tab="home" data-route="home" tabindex="-1">For you</a>
    <a id="header-nav-movies" href="#movies" class="tab f nav-pill-item" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" data-tab="movies" data-route="movies" tabindex="-1">Movies</a>
    <a id="header-nav-series" href="#series" class="tab f nav-pill-item" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" data-tab="series" data-route="series" tabindex="-1">Shows</a>
    <a id="header-nav-search" href="#search" class="tab f nav-pill-item" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" data-tab="search" data-route="search" tabindex="-1">Search</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- Google TV Settings / Quick Actions Pill -->
  <nav class="pill icons">
    <span class="ico f" data-nav="true" data-nav-group="header" data-act="settings" tabindex="-1" title="Settings">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill="currentColor" d="M19.4 13a7.5 7.5 0 0 0 0-2l2.1-1.6-2-3.5-2.5 1a7.4 7.4 0 0 0-1.7-1L15 3h-4l-.4 2.7a7.4 7.4 0 0 0-1.7 1l-2.5-1-2 3.5L6.6 11a7.5 7.5 0 0 0 0 2l-2.1 1.6 2 3.5 2.5-1c.5.4 1.1.7 1.7 1L11 21h4l.4-2.7c.6-.3 1.2-.6 1.7-1l2.5 1 2-3.5L19.4 13zM13 15.5a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 0-7 3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7z" transform="translate(-1 0)"/></svg>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <!-- Optional Weather Chip (hidden by default) -->
  <span id="weather" class="f" data-act="weather" hidden></span>

  <!-- Live Google TV Clock -->
  <div id="clock">12:00</div>
</header>
```

#### Dual-Contract Design Benefits:
1. `id="top"` matches Google TV reference specification.
2. `class="app-header"` preserves compatibility with `navigation.js` (`CONFIG.headerSelector: '.app-header'`), `app.js` (`document.querySelector('.app-header')`), and adversarial tests (`tests/adversarial-ui-m1-stress.js`, `tests/adversarial-ui-m4-challenger2.js`).
3. Dual classes `.tab.f.nav-pill-item` support Google TV styles (`.tab`, `.tab.cur`, `.tab.focus`) while allowing `app.js` to select `.nav-pill-item`.
4. Labels "For you", "Movies", "Shows", "Search" give the exact authentic Google TV copy.
5. In `app/js/app.js`, add `initClock()` to update `#clock` via pure `.textContent` every 10 seconds.
6. In `app/js/navigation.js` and `app/js/app.js`, toggle `document.body.classList.toggle('scrolled', isScrolled)` so the header auto-hides with `transform: translateY(-20px); opacity: 0` when scrolling down shelves.

